Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.58,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&\fs40}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.79,0:00:09.29,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I'm a soldier - that means I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.49,0:00:12.69,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Both a defendant and the judge
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.49,0:00:18.09,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I am standing on both ends of the flame
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.77,0:00:22.87,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Rounding curves
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.07,0:00:25.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Overtaking life and death,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.77,0:00:31.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,I run and fight with false shadows
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.97,0:00:38.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,No matter how many threads of\Ndeception are woven together,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.67,0:00:46.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,The truth shall illuminate\Nthe face of light
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.17,0:00:49.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your tears for the day
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.27,0:00:53.27,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,When our pain is far behind
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.67,0:00:56.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,On your feet, come with me
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.57,0:00:59.77,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We are soldiers stand or die
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.07,0:01:02.97,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save your fears, take your place
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.17,0:01:06.17,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Save them for the judgement day
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.47,0:01:09.37,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Fast and free, follow me
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.67,0:01:14.67,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,Time to make the sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.87,0:01:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,900,,We rise or fall
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.47,0:02:20.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Reporting from above the Kyushu Radio Tower.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.77,0:02:25.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A massive evacuation operation\Nconducted by the SDF began five days ago
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.27,0:02:29.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,with the discovery of an unexploded\Nshell at a subway construction site.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.87,0:02:32.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There was suspicion that the shell was a\Ntactical nuclear weapon from the Great War.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.87,0:02:34.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The SDF has finally succeeded in evacuating
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.07,0:02:39.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the 35 million people living within\Na 30 kilometre radius of the shell.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.81,0:02:44.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,A select few experts speculate that this may\Nbe another act of terrorism by the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.41,0:02:47.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,With the media still having received\Nno explanation from the government,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.41,0:02:50.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Fukuoka has the feel of a city under martial law,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.51,0:02:54.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,as part of the city sealed off by the SDF.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.11,0:02:59.52,Sign - Copy,,525,0,475,,{\b1\i1}Abandoned \N City{\b0\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.53,0:03:06.47,Sign,,300,0,790,,{\fs52}{\c&H0079FF&\3c&H000000&\b1}Inbound Routes Closed{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.53,0:03:06.47,Sign,,300,0,425,,{\fs52}{\c&H0079FF&\3c&H000000&\b1}Due to Bomb Disposal{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.89,0:03:14.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Martial law, huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.99,0:03:19.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The government's response may not be ideal,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.99,0:03:22.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but it's not like all of its powers\Nwere transferred to the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.79,0:03:23.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.19,0:03:27.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Although we know Kuze's camouflaged\Nship sank off the coast of Dejima,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.09,0:03:31.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we still can't say whether\Nany plutonium was on the ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.69,0:03:38.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's also still uncertain whether the refugees\Nreally triggered the massive blackout.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.59,0:03:43.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The populace continues to vent their anger\Nat the refugees against the government,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.59,0:03:47.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,so the government continues to throw its support\Nbehind any plans that will force the refugees' removal.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.49,0:03:53.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No one is pausing to think\Nabout where this all leads.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.09,0:03:57.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Even if the Cabinet Intelligence Agency's\Nmanipulation of information is the cause of this,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.59,0:04:00.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the rumours presently circulating\Nwill not just disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.49,0:04:05.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Batou, what's the matter with the Major?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.19,0:04:09.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wrote in my report that she's been acting a bit strange\Nsince she dove into Kuze's cyberbrain on Dejima, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.59,0:04:13.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right now, we have to focus on\Ndismantling the nuclear bomb.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.39,0:04:15.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Cabinet Intelligence Agency\Nis already moving to control the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.75,0:04:18.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,operation at the scene,\Nusing media coverage control as an excuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.59,0:04:19.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I will negotiate with the Prime Minister
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.99,0:04:23.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and see if she will give us the authority to\Ninvestigate the Cabinet Intelligence Agency.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.09,0:04:26.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When there's only circumstantial evidence?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.09,0:04:33.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The SDF is poised to invade. The Prime Minister\Nalready has a major problem in Dejima, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.09,0:04:38.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,At this point, I doubt she'd agree to something
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.49,0:04:41.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that might become a national scandal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.29,0:04:47.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If we screw this up.\NSection 9 could get nailed again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.99,0:04:51.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's why I arranged it so that\Nyou guys can intervene at the site.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.69,0:04:53.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You'd better find something there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.79,0:05:03.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, Major, why do you think\Nthe refugees are still silent?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.99,0:05:07.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The truth has already silenced\Nitself before the phenomenon...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.64,0:05:09.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze must've determined that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.24,0:05:12.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,For now, he's keeping his silence
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.14,0:05:14.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and looking for a chance to\Nturn the tables again somewhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.54,0:05:18.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,while keeping the truth\Nhidden, even from the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.24,0:05:19.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Why do you think that?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.64,0:05:22.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Because I would do the same, if I were him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.89,0:05:30.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It seems your mind is elsewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.39,0:05:35.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's true that we're here because of you,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.99,0:05:40.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but it's not like we're so helpless\Nthat we can't support you, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.49,0:05:44.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.09,0:05:47.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm not entirely displeased with your sentiment.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.69,0:05:54.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bomer, you and Pazu will participate in\Nthe bomb disposal operation as planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.79,0:05:56.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Saitou, you come with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.69,0:05:58.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, what's up with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.19,0:05:59.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Aren't we all going in?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.59,0:06:02.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have an idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.19,0:06:06.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Besides, I have something I want you to do for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.41,0:06:13.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Has the Japanese Miracle been deployed?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.91,0:06:14.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.91,0:06:16.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The deployment is already complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.31,0:06:17.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.21,0:06:21.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The results are unfortunate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.31,0:06:24.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,As soon as the bomb disposal\Noperation is complete,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.71,0:06:29.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll call a press conference\Nto announce the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.81,0:06:34.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After that, the SDF will most\Nlikely be able to invade Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.11,0:06:37.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Prime Minister, as I indicated in my report,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.11,0:06:41.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the possibility that the refugees\Nactually possess plutonium is minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.61,0:06:44.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It is most likely that the Cabinet Intelligence\NAgency has caused this situation to come to pass.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.91,0:06:50.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I would like you to help me to temporarily\Ndelay the SDF invasion of Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.21,0:06:51.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I read your report.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.21,0:06:56.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, we're already out of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.41,0:06:59.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Based on our information from Russian authorities,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.61,0:07:03.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the government is poised to act on\Nthe assumption that the plutonium
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.21,0:07:05.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,is already present in Dejima.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.11,0:07:07.51,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I don't mean to sound presumptuous,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.61,0:07:10.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but isn't that exactly what the\NCabinet Intelligence Agency wants?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.81,0:07:15.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No one wants it to happen,\Nbut the end result of an SDF invasion
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.11,0:07:16.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,is a war with the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.61,0:07:21.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Please, reconsider using the\Nreport in the Cabinet meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.11,0:07:25.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If only I had seen this earlier...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.11,0:07:31.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Public Safety Section 9 was my last trump card.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.00,0:07:39.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Chief Aramaki, please remain\Non alert for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.20,0:07:42.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.87,0:07:55.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Reports from Squads 6 and 13.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.07,0:07:58.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They are in position on the top floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.87,0:07:59.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.77,0:08:01.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're Public Safety Section 9,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.17,0:08:04.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're here at the Prime Minister's orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.27,0:08:06.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We haven't heard anything about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.37,0:08:07.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Don't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.77,0:08:10.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It happens a lot out in the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.67,0:08:11.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Doesn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.07,0:08:14.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Prime Minister's signature, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.67,0:08:15.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.67,0:08:18.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We just want our technicians on the front lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.57,0:08:20.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It can't be helped. Take them.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.47,0:08:21.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.57,0:08:27.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, what are you going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.67,0:08:30.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have business with that bureaucrat over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.77,0:08:32.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.77,0:08:36.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're on the verge of losing our\Njobs, thanks to you,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.67,0:08:39.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but there are two or three things I have to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.47,0:08:41.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Go right ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.21,0:08:46.16,Sign,,0,0,200,,{\b1}Kyushu Radio{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.05,0:08:52.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So that's it, huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.05,0:08:55.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We spent five days on the structural analysis.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.05,0:08:57.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We're finally about to begin\Nthe disposal operation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.05,0:09:00.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They're from Section 9,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.45,0:09:02.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,if there's something you\Ncan have them do, use them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.85,0:09:03.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.55,0:09:06.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,"To Kayabuki with love"?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.56,0:09:07.10,Sign,,450,0,920,,{\b1\fs50\c&H0000FF&}Kayabuki{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.75,0:09:09.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Talk about poor taste.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.65,0:09:15.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Similar messages were written on the\Nnosecones of Fatman, and also Scud missiles.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.05,0:09:16.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So they're copying America?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.65,0:09:19.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No idea. Couldn't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.65,0:09:22.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What are the Geiger counter readings?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.65,0:09:23.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They're positive.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.85,0:09:27.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But it doesn't seem as though they had the\Ntechnology or the time to build a nuclear warhead.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.35,0:09:29.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So it's just a plutonium bomb?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.65,0:09:30.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.75,0:09:32.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But if it were to detonate,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.16,0:09:34.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the area within a 30 kilometre radius\Nwould be contaminated with radiation.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.06,0:09:38.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We had no choice but to freeze it\Nwhile we evacuated the citizens
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.86,0:09:40.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and deployed the Japanese Miracle.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.66,0:09:42.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There was no timer?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.66,0:09:43.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Fortunately, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.96,0:09:45.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.26,0:09:49.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But there are at least two detonation systems,\None linked to a vibration-based pressure sensor,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.26,0:09:53.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and another to a photo-conductor.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.66,0:09:57.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Wait, the inner lid also has something.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.56,0:10:00.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you really just Public Safety?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.46,0:10:02.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,During the Great War, I was with the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.36,0:10:05.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, I was more of a specialist\Nin setting up bombs back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.42,0:10:14.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's kind of appropriate to have\Nour talk up here, while a nuclear
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.97,0:10:17.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,warhead's being dismantled right below\Nus, don't you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.86,0:10:23.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, how far do you intend to take this?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.26,0:10:25.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,To take what?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.26,0:10:27.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,How much worse are you going\Nto make the refugee situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.86,0:10:32.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You should ask the refugees or military analysts.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.26,0:10:34.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm not the expert.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.76,0:10:36.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.26,0:10:40.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Creating a medium who will give rise to mimics...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.66,0:10:43.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's your old field of research.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.06,0:10:49.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This society already contains factors that make\Nit easy for situations like that to develop.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.96,0:10:57.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,After all, human history has been shaped by those\Nwith power, who have "programed" myths and legends.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.16,0:10:59.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In a world such as this,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.26,0:11:04.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,a megalomaniac, whose desire to show off\Nbecame bloated without anyone noticing,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.96,0:11:08.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,wanted to produce a hero bigger than himself,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.56,0:11:15.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Weren't the Individual Eleven a fake stand\Nalone complex created by a criminal like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.66,0:11:17.36,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.46,0:11:19.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What an interesting story.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.85,0:11:22.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Hey, you fox.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.55,0:11:27.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But you're still second-rate.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.01,0:11:34.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Turn off the lights.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.61,0:11:38.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Isn't the lid loose?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.91,0:11:39.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.01,0:11:40.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.91,0:11:42.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,One parallel reflective switch.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.01,0:11:44.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.01,0:11:45.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Inserting mirror,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.40,0:11:51.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I have cut all the photo-conductive material.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.40,0:11:55.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,This model is an implosion-type nuclear bomb.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.60,0:12:00.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So it's their way of saying that\Nthey chose not to make the bomb.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.10,0:12:02.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,even though they had the time and technology,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.62,0:12:13.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.92,0:12:17.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Another retrieval team just went through here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.92,0:12:19.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.62,0:12:30.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Bomer, what is your impression\Nof the bomb's structure?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.02,0:12:35.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It presents the whole "message from the refugees"\Nact, but there's something strange about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.82,0:12:36.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.72,0:12:40.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The explosive is the M-112\Nthat's used by the American army.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.72,0:12:44.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's not the C-4 that the\Nrefugees have been using.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.42,0:12:45.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.42,0:12:48.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You guys stay there until it's defused,\Nand then join the transfer unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.62,0:12:51.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But we still haven't found material evidence that\Nleads back to the Cabinet Intelligence Agency...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.52,0:12:53.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What you've found is enough for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.82,0:12:54.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.62,0:13:00.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you mean, I'm second-rate?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.42,0:13:07.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We met a stand alone type hacker genius before.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.87,0:13:13.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I can't help but compare the\Nphenomenon he caused with this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.57,0:13:21.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When I compare him with the guys who killed themselves\Nhere, they don't seem all that impressive anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.47,0:13:26.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then we investigated the\NIndividual Eleven's external memory
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.37,0:13:30.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and discovered they were only mimics\Nwho appeared because of the virus.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.27,0:13:32.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.47,0:13:36.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They ended up acting as thought-guidance devices
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.67,0:13:44.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that some criminal made, using the name of\Nthe group who occupied the Chinese embassy.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.97,0:13:51.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The bastard who spread the virus probably\Nconsiders himself a damn good hacker, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.87,0:13:56.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Are you trying to imply that I'm\Nthe one who created the virus?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.17,0:13:57.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I didn't say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.64,0:14:01.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then what do you want me to talk about?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.84,0:14:06.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you think about the Individual Eleven?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.44,0:14:11.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.64,0:14:17.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Supposing that the Individual Eleven\Nappeared because of a virus, like you said,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.14,0:14:26.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,could you not say that they are as ingenious\Nas the stand alone type hacker, if not more so,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.54,0:14:30.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,or even heroes,\Nfor continually expanding the situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.24,0:14:34.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They {\i1}did{\i} spread their thinking\Nwith the mass-suicide performance.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.34,0:14:36.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But whose heroes did they become?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.04,0:14:38.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Japanese citizens?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.74,0:14:39.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No way.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.23,0:14:44.00,Sign,,0,1500,300,,{\fs52}{\b1}To the \N Nameless Eleven{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.00,0:14:46.00,Sign,,0,1200,200,,{\fs52}{\b1}To the \N Nameless Eleven{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.00,0:14:48.81,Sign,,0,1000,100,,{\fs52}{\b1}To the \N Nameless Eleven{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.15,0:14:48.81,Sign,,0,1200,950,,{\fs52}{\b1}Death!{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.85,0:14:43.00,Sign,,0,0,650,,{\fs52}{\b1}To the Individual Eleven{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.01,0:14:44.63,Sign,,0,0,550,,{\fs52}{\b1}To the Individual Eleven{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.63,0:14:46.47,Sign,,400,0,500,,{\fs52}{\b1}To the Individual Eleven{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.47,0:14:48.81,Sign,,550,0,450,,{\fs52}{\b1}To the Individual Eleven{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.64,0:14:45.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,At best, they're clowns who gave the refugee\Nproblem an opportunity to deteriorate.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.64,0:14:48.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In reality, their deaths\Nhave already been forgotten.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.54,0:14:51.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.14,0:14:54.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But suppose the true purpose of the phenomenon\Nwas to bring about the current situation
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.44,0:14:58.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and not to keep these deaths in people's memories,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.24,0:15:04.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,then could you not say that this criminal who produced\Nthe Individual Eleven is the hacker genius?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.04,0:15:08.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yeah, I can't deny that, unfortunately.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.84,0:15:13.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'm still a bit skeptical when\Nyou call him a genius, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.24,0:15:17.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The profile I can see from the Eleven's\Nthoughts and the virus's characteristics
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.44,0:15:21.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,is that of a particularist who\Nwas possessed by the desire
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.64,0:15:23.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to escape his sense of inferiority.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.24,0:15:27.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,In the end, you can't impress people
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.64,0:15:30.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,if you're just forcing your own ideas onto them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.24,0:15:35.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Unless there's something like a strong\Nbelief, be it benevolent or malevolent,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.74,0:15:38.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,you can't become a genius or a hero.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.44,0:15:40.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Belief...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.94,0:15:41.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.94,0:15:43.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,At least, that's what I believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.14,0:15:45.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And one more thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.74,0:15:49.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The one single factor that's absolutely necessary.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.14,0:15:51.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Luck: it would be indispensable.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.04,0:15:54.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Oh? Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.84,0:15:56.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.64,0:15:59.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,When it comes right down to it,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.14,0:16:02.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the existence of heroes and geniuses pretty\Nmuch depends on a third party's point of view.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.24,0:16:08.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,To make a hero into a hero,\Nyou first need the spectators response.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.64,0:16:14.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And that response can make or break a hero...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.24,0:16:16.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and that's all dependent on luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.74,0:16:18.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.74,0:16:20.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,That is an interesting theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.94,0:16:24.74,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Still, I had no idea you\Nwere this much of a talker.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.44,0:16:27.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is that a compliment?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.64,0:16:30.14,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You can take it as one.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.04,0:16:35.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then since I'm being complimented,\NI'll mention one more thing:
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.24,0:16:39.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the x-factor in this incident,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.17,0:16:55.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's on the top floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.87,0:17:07.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze Hideo was the only one among\Nthe Eleven who didn't kill himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.57,0:17:11.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,He then disappeared,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.17,0:17:14.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and by the time he reappeared,\Nhe was the leader of the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.77,0:17:17.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What a strange story.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.77,0:17:19.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is this a coincidence?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.87,0:17:22.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Or something that was set\Nup from the very beginning?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.47,0:17:28.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Since his behaviour was the total\Nopposite of the others in the Eleven,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.67,0:17:31.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,it must be the x-factor you refer to.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.67,0:17:33.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But it can still be seen as something
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.77,0:17:36.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,that effectively contributes to the\Nmovement towards the refugees removal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.27,0:17:40.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,While his actions are of a different sort,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.57,0:17:44.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,the fact is that they are guiding the\Nsituation towards a similar conclusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.07,0:17:51.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So, it seems the perpetrator masterfully\Nproduced even the x-factor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.87,0:17:53.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,So that's how you'll put it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.27,0:17:57.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Well, his actions could be said to be\Nspeeding up the removal of the refugees.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.77,0:18:01.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The Nagasaki blackout lent further emphasis
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.67,0:18:04.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,to the camouflaged ship chase that\Nwas streamed across the network.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.27,0:18:08.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,And now, there's the nuclear\Nbomb right underneath us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.67,0:18:14.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The government has no choice but to take the matter\Nseriously, now that Kuze has taken things this far.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.07,0:18:19.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,However, was it really Kuze who did all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.77,0:18:24.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Isn't it actually some trumped-up act by\Nthe perpetrator who is "producing" him?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.27,0:18:30.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Furthermore, couldn't you say that this\N"producer" is aiding Kuze without realising it
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.27,0:18:34.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and is starting to mimic Kuze's actions?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.27,0:18:35.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.67,0:18:38.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Kuze returned to Dejima from Ostrov Iturup,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.97,0:18:41.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but he didn't have the plutonium on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.97,0:18:44.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Under normal circumstances,\Nhe would've wanted to tell the refugees
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.57,0:18:47.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and do damage control.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.07,0:18:51.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Yet a terrorist attack involving\Nplutonium has now occurred.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.37,0:18:52.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Then what?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.37,0:18:58.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Would he go along with the plans of his\N"producer" and call the bluff, declaring war?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.17,0:19:02.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,But he didn't do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.27,0:19:04.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Right now, he's keeping quiet,\Nmaking the refugees stay quiet,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.57,0:19:07.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,and waiting for a chance to turn the tables.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.67,0:19:15.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Or rather, isn't it actually Kuze who\Ngained a trump card by keeping quiet?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.17,0:19:18.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If Kuze, who was originally just an x-factor,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.17,0:19:22.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,is actually the true genius... the true hero...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.87,0:19:25.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,isn't it possible that the one\Nwho thought he was producing Kuze
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.97,0:19:30.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,has somehow become Kuze's mimicker?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.81,0:20:03.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I'll leave the rest to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.01,0:20:04.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Roger.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.07,0:20:14.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,They had faith in a fabricated\Nbelief and even committed suicide.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.17,0:20:18.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,yet they couldn't become anyone's heroes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.17,0:20:21.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I wonder where their ghosts are wandering now.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.84,0:20:44.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Major, did the plutonium retrieval go well?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.74,0:20:45.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The operation is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.44,0:20:47.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.74,0:20:49.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Using your external memory as a guide,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.74,0:20:52.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I tried to discuss Kuze in my own way,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.34,0:20:53.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but I wonder if it went as well as I hoped.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.44,0:20:56.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It did.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.04,0:20:59.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'll go directly to Spring-8 from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.04,0:21:05.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,The intelligence specialists obsession with realism\Nleft evidence, and it will be their undoing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.74,0:21:09.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,if this plutonium matches what we found\Nin the Shinjuku nuclear power plant,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.04,0:21:13.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,we will be able to prove that this was\Nthe Cabinet Intelligence Agency's doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.54,0:21:14.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.40,0:21:18.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Gouda.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.60,0:21:22.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Like Kuze, we haven't given up hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.70,0:21:24.10,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.24,0:21:30.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I forgot to ask you one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.64,0:21:33.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I doubt there would be\Nanother outbreak of the virus,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.04,0:21:37.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,but we don't know the one remaining\Nfactor that'll cause symptoms to appear.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.64,0:21:40.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,We'd like to make a vaccine just in case.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.14,0:21:42.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If it were up to you,\Nwhat would you make the last factor?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.04,0:21:47.54,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,If I were the one responsible,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.54,0:21:56.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I would find a host who was a\Nvirgin before becoming a cyborg.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.74,0:21:58.24,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.20,0:22:03.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,It's an absolute necessity if you're\Nlooking for a willingness to die
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.40,0:22:05.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in order to become a hero for the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.10,0:22:10.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Of course, whether there would be people\Nwith that rare quality was a wager,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.80,0:22:12.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,You bastard...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.30,0:22:14.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,There's a limit to how sick\Nof a bastard you can be.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.62,0:22:16.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:16.72,0:22:19.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Actually, I'm a virgin as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.12,0:22:23.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Our talk was delightful.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.32,0:22:24.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No, it was insightful.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.72,0:22:25.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I thank you for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.02,0:22:29.82,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,My battle is not over yet, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.92,0:22:32.52,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Whether you people will stop me first,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.62,0:22:35.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,or my goals will reach their conclusion
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.72,0:22:39.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,will depend on the x-factor.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.42,0:22:41.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.66,0:23:10.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Finding out a galaxy
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.01,0:23:14.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,of planets and stars within me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.11,0:23:17.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,Listening to each of them
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.81,0:23:21.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,singing the same silent melody.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.26,0:23:25.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I've never seen such beauty
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.76,0:23:28.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,in possibility...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:29.06,0:23:32.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,No smack of doubt or fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.26,0:23:34.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(Wake up)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.86,0:23:36.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,I hear a voice.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.69,0:23:39.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,(And show the light)
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.45,0:23:39.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,150,,hear a voice calling out to me.
